From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hugo <LinuxBoy-96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:15:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Implement text-overflow (ellipsis and string markers)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rebased from DioxusLabs/blitz#893 (head 51fcffbe) onto the series.
Overflowing lines in a clipping inline root (`overflow` other than
`visible`) are cut at a glyph boundary and end with the `text-overflow`
marker: `…` for `ellipsis`, the given string otherwise. Paint-time
truncation (css-overflow §5.2 defines the ellipsis as a rendering
effect): layout, scrollWidth, selection and hit testing keep the full
text.

- blitz-dom: after line breaking and alignment, `layout::text_overflow`
  finds the lines wider than the content box and shapes the marker with
  the block container's style. For an anonymous inline root (Blitz wraps
  inline content in scroll containers), the block is the parent.
- blitz-paint: `stroke_text` drops the glyphs past the cut and draws the
  marker once after the kept glyphs, in the block's colour. Decorations
  stop at the cut, and the marker is undecorated, as in Chrome. A focused
  contenteditable paints as `clip`.

Only the inline-end side is handled (no RTL start-side marker).
